-- CC_0350 - 2026-11-03 US House: record the races AP has called.
--
-- Wave 2. 377 of the 435 US House races now carry a winner, each marked
-- `result_certainty = 'called'` and sourced to the AP race call that named the person. Same
-- feed and same method as CC_0339 (the Senate), scaled from 35 races to 435.
--
-- ⚠ NOTHING HERE IS CERTIFIED. Every row is `called`. Not one of the 435 races has
-- `isCertified: true` in AP's own metadata as of 2026-11-04. A later pass upgrades each row
-- against that state's own canvass.
--
-- ⚠ THIS SEATS NOBODY. Nothing here writes `office_terms`. Seating is a separate migration,
-- at the date CC_0348 established for the federal tier: 2027-01-03.
--
-- ============================================================================================
-- THE ARITHMETIC
-- ============================================================================================
--   435  US House races on the 2026-11-03 ballot, ours and AP's alike
--  - 57  AP has not called: 56 "Too Early to Call" + 1 Louisiana runoff
--  -----
--   378  AP calls carrying exactly one winner
--  -  1  TX-22 - AP's winner is a person this database does not hold (see below)
--  ----
--   377  rows written here
--
-- ============================================================================================
-- 🔴 TX-22 IS LEFT OUT, AND IT IS THE REASON THIS FILE IS NOT A NAME JOIN
-- ============================================================================================
-- AP's TX-22 winner is **Trever Nehls** (AP candidateID 170023, GOP, 51.82%). AP's own
-- metadata lists the INCUMBENT of that seat separately as **Troy Nehls** (candidateID 68186).
-- They are different people - identical twin brothers. Troy Nehls did not seek re-election;
-- Trever Nehls won the March 2026 primary to succeed him.
--
-- 🔴 OUR `race_candidates` FOR TX-22 CARRIES TROY NEHLS, NOT TREVER. We hold no Trever Nehls
-- row at all. A last-name match therefore lands the win on the sitting congressman, and the
-- site would report that Troy Nehls was re-elected to a seat he did not run for.
--
-- This is the Lindsey Graham trap from CC_0339 wearing the other face: there the stale row was
-- a LOSER we would have invented, here it is a WINNER we would have misattributed.
-- ▶ A NAME THAT MATCHES IS NOT A PERSON THAT MATCHES. The detector that caught it compares
--   AP's winner candidateID against AP's own incumbent candidateID and flags a shared surname
--   across different ids. It found exactly two races, TX-22 and IL-04. IL-04 is correct:
--   AP "Patty Garcia" id 170445 beat incumbent "Jesus Garcia" id 16407, and our row IS Patty
--   Garcia, a distinct person - so the flag is a prompt to look, not a verdict.
-- ▶ FOLLOW-UP, NOT PART OF THIS FILE: seed Trever Nehls as the TX-22 candidate, correct Troy
--   Nehls' candidacy row, then record the call. Troy Nehls still holds the seat until
--   2027-01-03 and his `is_incumbent` flag is right as it stands.
--
-- ============================================================================================
